<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila mining shares sub-index up on peso weakness.</title>
<headline>Manila mining shares sub-index up on peso weakness.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine mining shares sub-index gained in midtrade on Thursday as gold exporters were seen benefiting from the peso's weakness, traders said.</p>
<p>&quot;The peso is at 29 to the dollar. Even if the price of gold has declined the past few weeks, the loss will be compensated by the higher foreign exchange rate,&quot; said Henry Ong, analyst at Sapphire Securities.</p>
<p>The mining sub-index surged 295.21 points, or 8.0 percent to 3,986.25. It posted the biggest gain among the six sub-indices.</p>
</text>
